	(text "Notes:\n- Design rule: this hexpansion never powers the badge (HISTORY.md section 4.5).\n- Pull-ups on badge-facing lines go to 3V3_BADGE, never +3V3. No pull-ups on BADGE_SDA/SCL (badge has them).\n- Firmware: tri-state SPI_MISO and BADGE_IRQ until BADGE_SENSE (GPIO28) reads the badge rail live.\n- Firmware: do not enable internal pull-ups on BADGE_SDA/SCL (GPIO24/25).\n- Badge reset: LS_A drives RUN through U11, an open-drain buffer powered from 3V3_BADGE (no leak when the badge is off).\n- HS_G/HS_H are crossed (HS_H=CS on GPIO21, HS_G=SCK on GPIO22) to match the badge mirror driver (tested on all six ports).\n- Spare GPIOs (no-connect): 3, 4, 5, 8, 9, 10, 11. microSD dropped.\n- HDMI DDC (EDID) not connected: output is fixed 640x480@60. HPD is read on GPIO2.\n- Decoupling: C1-C7 follow the Raspberry Pi minimal design (pins 44/45 and 53/54 share a cap).\n- U9 (PSRAM) and U10 (EEPROM) are DNP. C20 (PSRAM decoupling) and R7 (CS pull-up) are fitted.\n- HSTX lanes: D2=GPIO12/13, CK=14/15, D1=16/17, D0=18/19 (+ on even pin), as pio-testcard firmware."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 539 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
